{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261124T184311Z-f172abe0", "ts": "2026-11-24T18:45:10Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.9.1-dev", "branch": "fix/report-bug-triage-sync", "build": "88c92a5b7209"}, "body": {"base_commit": "88c92a5b7209f951ded0cb597c4c536ba04eef05", "base_tree": "5a5fdb8b8d6044d2baf0039d8cfa7f5440586b38", "head_tree": "d0f502602a91ed4d1a16481c9ce8cfeda08fce94", "head_commit": "9b5fc560c39b26a1002821ad5973044199db768d", "dispatch_commit": "9b5fc560c39b26a1002821ad5973044199db768d", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["plugin/skills/report-bug/SKILL.md"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/changes/report-bug-triage-sync.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md", "plugin/skills/report-bug/SKILL.md"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/changes/report-bug-triage-sync.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "warning", "title": "Triage sync step leaves its own failure mode open: a failed `backlog sync` is not addressed, and the new step has no pin", "recommendation": "The new step says to run `prawduct-hook backlog sync --repo <backlog_service_repo>` and then `cache-query unstaged`, because an empty answer from a stale cache looks like an empty intake. It never says what to do when the sync fails (network, auth, rate limit). In that case the model goes straight on to `cache-query`, which still answers `ok` with the stale rows plus `sync_error`, or exits 6 `unavailable` on a scope that has never synced (`plugin/lib/upstream_probes.py` `_intake_reading`; `plugin/skills/backlog/cache-reads.md` \"Reading the answer\"). Either way the empty list gets misread just as before, and the report-bug skill never mentions `sync_error`, `unavailable`/exit 6, or cache-reads.md. Add one clause: if the sync exits non-zero, or the listing carries `sync_error` or exits 6, say so to the operator and do not report the intake as empty. A pointer to `skills/backlog/cache-reads.md` \"Reading the answer\" would also do. The new ordering is a behavioural instruction, and nothing pins it. Add a presence/order assertion next to `TestTheIntakeAsksForWhatDecidesAChunkRow` in `tests/test_backlog_upstream.py`: the receiving-side section names `backlog sync --repo` before `cache-query unstaged`, and both are ops the CLI accepts. Then a later trim of this paragraph cannot silently bring back the stale-cache misread.", "files": ["plugin/skills/report-bug/SKILL.md"], "scope": "instance", "fid": "R-1"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 1, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "Governing-Artifact Reconciliation: nothing to reconcile", "recommendation": "No live plan claims `fix/report-bug-triage-sync` (manifest scope unbound), so there are no `governed_by:` dispositions to check against the diff. record_lint reports governed-by-gap 0. No edit wanted.", "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "Factual claims in the new step verified against code", "recommendation": "Three claims checked. `backlog sync --repo owner/repo` is a real op (`plugin/lib/backlog/cli.py` `_run_sync`). `cache-query` opens the store without revalidating, so it makes no network call (`plugin/bin/prawduct-hook`, the ephemeral read-only set comment). The advisory count is offline by construction from `cachequery.unstaged_items` (`plugin/lib/upstream_probes.py`). The skill has no `allowed-tools` restriction, so the added command needs no permission entry. Sibling descriptions of the intake query (adapter-mode.md:136, backlog-service-data-model.md:217, api-contract.md:433) point to the skill for the procedure, and the change does not make them false. test-status is current (tree-valid). verify-coverage is